The two mid vowels can be raised in certain [[Phonetic environment|phonetic environments]], but no [[Minimal pair|minimal pairs]], words differing in only one [[phoneme]], are known to contrast getween high and mid vowels. The status of vowel length is uncertain, as no minimal pairs exist for this contrast, although certain words have consistently lengthened vowels (e.g. {{Lang|spn|pesaːsep}} 'night'), and others consistently without (e.g. {{Lang|spn|kelasma}} 'fish'). Vowels are written as in Spanish.<ref name=":0">{{Cite book|last=van Gysel|first=Jens|title=Temporal Predicative Particles in Sanapaná and the Enlhet-Enenlhet Language Family (Paraguay): A Descriptive and Comparative Study|publisher=Leiden University|year=2017|isbn=|location=|pages=27–38|url=https://etnolinguistica.wdfiles.com/local--files/tese%3Agysel-2017/Jens_Van_Gysel_2017_Temporal_Predicative_Particles_in_Sanapana.pdf}}</ref>{{Reference page|page=29}}

